menu "BYOK clock mode"

    config BYOK_CLOCK_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "No-host idle timeout before switching to the on-device CLOCK screen (ms)"
        default 30000
        range 1000 3600000
        help
            byok_modes.h's CLOCK mode (a device-local PCF8563-driven clock
            face, byok_clock component) is entered automatically once this
            many milliseconds pass with no frame received from a connected
            host -- covering BOTH "the host went away/asleep" and "no host
            has ever connected since boot" with the one mechanism, since
            byok_clock's own idle timer starts at the same t=0 either way
            (esp_timer's own boot-relative clock) rather than needing a
            separate "at boot" special case. Any frame received from a host
            afterwards switches the device straight back to DASHBOARD_USB
            (byok_clock_notify_host_frame(), called from app_main.c's
            byok_on_frame() on every frame that reaches the dispatcher) --
            this value only controls how long the device waits before
            giving up on a host that has gone quiet, not how long CLOCK
            itself stays up once entered.

            30 s (the default) is long enough that a host's own brief
            connect/HELLO/GET_INFO handshake never trips it, short enough
            that unplugging the cable (or the host app quitting) shows a
            useful screen well within the time an owner glances at the
            device expecting either a dashboard or the time.

endmenu
